course: dictionary
lesson: 15750
title: Tried: effort, testing and more
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Tried» is the past of the verb «try». Try means to make an effort, or to test something to see what happens. Tries, trying and tried are all forms of the same word, so tried is for something that has already happened.
explain: «I tried to lift the box, but it was too heavy.» Here tried means I made an effort. The words «but it was too heavy» show that the effort did not finish the job, but the effort still counts as trying.
explain: Tried can have other meanings. «I tried sushi» means I tasted it to see what it is like. «She tried on the shoes» means she put them on to check the fit. Look at the words next to tried to find out which meaning fits.
explain: «Tried and tested» is a phrase that means something has been proven to work well. A tried and tested recipe is one that many people have made successfully.
fact: Tried is the past form of try: try, tries, tried, trying.
fact: «Tried» means made an effort to do something, as in «I tried my best».
fact: «Tried» can also mean tasted something to see what it is like, or put on clothes to see if they fit.
fact: «Tried and tested» means proven to work well.
fact: In a law court, «tried» means judged, as in «He was tried for theft».
exercise: «I tried to lift the box, but it was too heavy.» What does tried mean here? | Tasted something | Judged in a court of law | Put on clothes to see if they fit | *Made an effort to do something
exercise: «She tried on the shoes at the shop.» What does tried on mean? | Made a loud noise | *Put on clothes to see if they fit | Bought them without looking | Took them off and left
exercise: Which word is the past form of try? | try | *tried | trying | tries
test: «Sam tried sushi for the first time.» What does tried mean here? | Ran away from home | *Tasted something to see what it is like | Fell asleep on the sofa
test: Which phrase means something has been proven to work well? | Tried to hide | Tried out for a team | Tried on a hat | *Tried and tested
exam: «The court tried the man for theft.» What does tried mean here? | Put on a coat to see if it fits | Made an effort to climb a wall | *Judged in a court of law | Tasted something to see what it is like
